      "limitations": [
        "Each row bounds one isolated event/component fixture including CLI startup and setup; exclusive callback CPU is unavailable in the SDK.",
        "All registered event names and render components are checked; individual matcher branches have unmeasured callback coverage.",
        "The kit cannot retain session.append rows; both prompt and response pre-next paths are measured.",
        "classic.PreModelSwitch, classic.PostModelSwitch, classic.Stop, model.complete and model.fork were measured on a cloud VM (raw wait4 CPU, about 2.2 to 2.5 s each, mostly CLI startup); the other rows were measured on the Mac. All five land on the 3 s floor. model.complete and model.fork are dispatched through the scratch bridge, so they run the plugin's own handler with the plugin as origin. classic.StopFailure and ui.message (added by PLAY, whose report queued them for the Mac) were measured the same way on this VM and land at 4 s. classic.SessionStart (FIRST-MEETING) was measured the same way and lands at 4 s.",
        "The 33 targets 1.0's wiring added (M1's always-on hooks, the book's own controls, the skill cards) were measured 10-17 on a cloud VM with Claude Code 2.1.302 (raw wait4 CPU, 3.7 to 5.1 s each, mostly CLI startup), so they land at 5 to 7 s; on the same VM the Mac rows measured 3.7 to 4.3 s, so a slower host scales every row by COCO_CPU_SCALE, as the kit files are scaled."
      ],
